    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Find the probability that if 10 people sit around a table at random, 2 particular people will be seated together.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{2}{9}$",
      "worked": "Total circular arrangements: $9!$.\n\nTreat the 2 particular people as one unit. There are 9 units to arrange around the circle, giving $8!$ arrangements. The pair can be arranged internally in $2!$ ways.\n$$P(\\text{seated together})=\\frac{8!\\times2!}{9!}=\\frac29$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
